5. SCOPE OF WORK.

5.1.
All lead-based paint and asbestos abatement shall be conducted by a fully licensed and
insured contractor with expertise in the abatement of the stated materials (“Contractor”).
Lessee shall provide Lessor with copies of the Contractor’s licenses and training
certificates required under state and federal law as they relate to the abatement activities.
Lessee will provide the Contractor’s Scope of Work to Lessor for review.  Lessor retains
the right to require modification to the Scope of Work for any reason. Commencement
of abatement activities will not be permitted prior to Lessor’s written acceptance of the
Scope of Work.

5.2.
Lessee shall require all Contractor’s to execute a Right of Entry and Hold Harmless
Agreement, for any access to and from the Leased Premises, prior to any work being
conducted by such Contractor pursuant to this Lease, in a form acceptable and approved
by Lessor, to be approved in Lessor’s sole discretion.

6. LESSOR RESERVED RIGHTS.

6.1.
Lessor reserves the right to use, operate upon, maintain, repair, replace, or augment the
Leased Premises or relocate the Lessee, provided that said relocation does not
unreasonably interfere with Lessee's Use of the Leased Premises for the purposes set
forth in this section.  This Lease is subject and subordinate to any right which Lessor or
any easement holder, lessee, or licensee of Lessor may have in the Leased Premises.
Lessee shall not interfere with the maintenance or operation of the Reserved Facilities,
