11. ENVIRONMENTAL COMPLIANCE.

11.1. Lessee hereby agrees to defend (with counsel reasonably approved by Lessor), protect,
indemnify and hold the Lessor harmless from and against, and shall reimburse the
Lessor for, any and all costs (including, without limitation, reasonable attorney’s fees
and expenses), damages, penalties, fines, expenses or losses arising from any and all
claims, demands, losses, liabilities, fines, penalties, charges, causes of action, injury
to person, property, or natural resources, administrative and judicial proceedings and
orders, injunctive relief, judgments, remedial action requirements, enforcement
actions of any kind, but excluding, with respect to the Lessor, those arising out of the
negligence or willful misconduct of Lessor, arising directly or indirectly, in whole or
in part, out of or attributable to any Release (as hereinafter defined) or threatened
Release, whether foreseeable or unforeseeable, which (A) occurs during the Term and
is the result of an omission or action by the Lessee or (B) occurs after the expiration
of the Term but is nevertheless the result of an action or omission by Lessee during
the Term. For purposes of this Paragraph 9.1, “Lessor” shall include Lessor, its agents,
contractors, employees and invitees.
